# The Dockerfile copies `mobile/`, `spike/` and `assets/` explicitly rather than
# `COPY . .`, so this file is a second line of defence, not the only one.

# The retired engine and the contaminated corpus were archived outside this
# repository on 2026-08-22 and are no longer present. These rules stay as a
# backstop in case anything is ever restored by accident.
_retired_contaminated/
scenario/
app/
core/
policy/
tools/
mallow_preview.html
run_local_demo.sh

.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*-key.json
*credentials*.json
service-account*.json
.gcloud/
.config/gcloud/
.firebase/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Local full-resolution masters; the product uses assets/art/*.webp.
assets/art/Original/

.git/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# 🔴 The live journal — a person's own records.
#
# The rule here used to be `data/out/`, which was the generated-corpus
# directory of a retired design. It is not the directory the product writes to;
# that is `data/live/`, and it was never covered. Three documents have said
# since 2026-08-22 that all three ignore files excluded it. They did not.
# Fixed 2026-08-23 by excluding the whole tree, which cannot drift again.
data/

# The demo seeder is COMMITTED, on purpose (戰略官 2026-08-23): a judge who
# cannot reproduce the autonomous leaf cannot verify the one thing this
# submission is about. `demo/seed.py` is a clean synthetic script and nothing
# else lives in there; what it *produces* goes to `data/`, which is ignored
# above. The Dockerfile's explicit COPY list keeps it out of the image without
# needing a rule here.

# The visual QA package — roughly 53MB of screenshots that settled the
# registration numbers (PRODUCT_DECISIONS 25: kept on the machine, out of the
# submission repository). The report itself is small and worth keeping.
qa/*
!qa/QA_REPORT.md

mobile/tests/
spike/voice/tests/

# 🔴 Runtime art is WebP (Q-37 r2). The PNGs stay in the repository as the
# source paintings and as what visual QA compares against, but no request can
# reach them any more: every reference in the template and in the service
# worker names the .webp. Shipping both would put 3.7MB of unreachable files
# into the image.
assets/art/*.png
